# Line endings are LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# This is load-bearing, not tidiness. Windows GitHub runners ship
# `core.autocrlf=true`, so without this file a Windows checkout converts every text file
# to CRLF — and `zig fmt --check` rejects CRLF outright. The result was a `fmt` step that
# reported *every* `.zig` file as "non-conforming formatting" on Windows while passing on
# Linux and macOS, which reads like a formatting problem in the code and is not one.
#
# The same conversion breaks the shell scripts (`bash` reads the `\r` as part of the
# command) and would silently alter `spec/schema.json`, which is vendored byte-for-byte
# from the specification repository and documented as unmodified.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Stated explicitly for the files where CRLF is not a cosmetic difference but a failure.
*.zig   text eol=lf
*.zon   text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
